::U2UA_L2_Q01::Cardiorespiratory endurance supports what? {=Sustained activity ~Only brief power ~Joint range only ~Reaction time}

::U2UA_L2_Q02::Which activity is primarily aerobic? {=A 30-minute brisk walk ~A 10-second sprint ~One explosive jump ~A brief maximal effort}

::U2UA_L2_Q03::Which activity is primarily anaerobic? {=A 10-second sprint ~Steady cycling ~A 20-minute walk ~Low-impact dancing}

::U2UA_L2_Q04::Exercise intensity means what? {=How hard the body is working ~How long activity lasts ~Which equipment is used ~How many weeks pass}

::U2UA_L2_Q05::Duration means what? {=How long activity lasts ~How hard the body works ~Heartbeats per minute ~Speech comfort}

::U2UA_L2_Q06::Heart rate is measured in what? {=Beats per minute ~Minutes per mile only ~RPE points ~Percent body composition}

::U2UA_L2_Q07::The 220 minus age calculation produces what? {=An estimated maximum heart rate ~An exact medical maximum ~A resting pulse ~A diagnosis}


